-- ============================================================================
-- 1. Domain-by-Domain Compositional Folding (Sheaf Gluing over Interface I)
-- ============================================================================
-- A glued two-domain conformation: local folds (c1, c2) that agree on their shared interface I.
GluedFold : (C1 C2 I : Type 0) → (C1 → I) → (C2 → I) → Type 0
GluedFold C1 C2 I r1 r2 = (p : C1 × C2) × (r1 (fst p) ≡ r2 (snd p))
